        <summary>Gets a value that indicates whether the DEX file is in an optimal state.</summary>
        <value><see langword="true" /> if the DEX file is in an optimal state; otherwise, <see langword="false" />.</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>Currently, an optimal state means that the file is compiled ahead of time with a profile or is fully compiled ahead of time. This does not require <see cref="P:Dalvik.SystemInterop.DexFile.OptimizationInfo.IsFullyCompiled" /> to be <see langword="true" />.</para>
          <para>See the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/libcore/+/de876a01b29230b877c9f408348c38a90ee724a5/dalvik/src/main/java/dalvik/system/DexFile.java">Android isOptimized source</a></format>.</para>
